{
  "name": "Your Step-by-Step Guide to a Smooth Bathroom Remodel",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Ready to transform your bathroom? A well-planned remodel can make a huge difference, and here's a general roadmap of how it usually goes. First, you'll define your scope and budget – what exactly do you want, and how much are you willing to spend? Then comes selecting the right contractor. You'll want someone who understands code compliance and can coordinate various trades. Once you've got your team, they'll review if any permits are needed for things like plumbing or electrical changes. After that, it's demolition time! This is when things get a bit messy, but it's exciting to see the old go. Next up are the 'rough-ins' for plumbing, electrical, and HVAC – getting all those behind-the-wall elements in place. This is usually followed by inspections to ensure everything is up to code. Then, the fun really starts with finish installation: tiles, vanity, fixtures, paint – bringing your vision to life! Finally, you'll do a walkthrough with your contractor to make sure everything is perfect. Depending on the complexity, a remodel can take 8 to 12 weeks, or up to 6 to 12 months for bigger projects. HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area, is here to help you every step of the way.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
